- Cite findings as file:line. Be concrete enough that a builder agent could apply fixes without rediscovering context.`

phase('Review')
const reviews = await pipeline(
  PRS,
  (p) =>
    agent(
      `Maintainer review of gastownhall/beads PR #${p.n} by ${p.author} (part of an author-clustered sweep).

Cluster context / hint for this PR: ${p.hint}

Gather, at minimum:
1. gh pr view ${p.n} --repo gastownhall/beads --json title,body,state,mergeable,maintainerCanModify,baseRefName,headRefName,statusCheckRollup,createdAt
2. Full review history: gh pr view ${p.n} --repo gastownhall/beads --json reviews,comments ; inline threads via gh api repos/gastownhall/beads/pulls/${p.n}/comments — identify exactly what any CHANGES_REQUESTED review demanded and check the CURRENT branch state for whether each demand was addressed (reviews may be stale).
3. The diff: gh pr diff ${p.n} --repo gastownhall/beads.
4. Supersession & drift: what has landed on upstream/main since the PR's base touching the same paths or solving the same problem (git -C bd-main log upstream/main --oneline -- <paths>; read suspicious merged diffs with git -C bd-main show). This cluster has known supersession suspects — take the hint seriously and compare actual diffs, not titles.
